  "body": "Hi,\r\n\r\nI have a scenario in wich a intraweb application must access serial port to work with a device connected to a serial port on each workstation. The serial device is setted in a fixed virtual COM Port and it is always the same model and vendor for all workstations. The user must grant permission when application wants access the port, so it works very good, but in this environment the application will be closed and opened many times at day, so user must always grant permission after he closes the browser, and sometimes user dont know wich port must be selected (normally first time is setted by IT staff). It would be very usefull for this scenario if there were a option `Allow Always` right like the **camera and mic**, and remember the permission for the **same domain**, so user must grant permission only one time for the same domain and later will not ask for permission and `.getPorts()` will return the previously allowed port. User could have a tiny button on the addressbar like btn for camera permission and may be there can revoke at any time.\r\n\r\nIt is acctually possible? and could this be an option, would be a good idea?\r\n\r\nUser experience is reduced due frecuently permission prompts.",
